; The load's base is select(c, %a, %b), and the store goes to %b. Using
; getUnderlyingObject (singular) on the select would return the select
; itself and miss the alias on %b. getUnderlyingObjects (plural) walks
; through the select, exposing both %a and %b as load roots; %b is then
; recognized as appearing in both the load and store sets and realign is
; rejected.
